   "kind": "plaintext",
   "value": "alloc::vec::Vec\n\nimpl<T, A> Vec<T, A>\npub fn push(&mut self, value: T)\nwhere\n    // Bounds from impl:\n    A: Allocator + Destruct,\n\n\nT = i32, A = Global\n\n\nAppends an element to the back of a collection.\n\nPanicsPanics if the new capacity exceeds isize::MAX bytes.\n\nExampleslet mut vec = vec![1, 2];\nvec.push(3);\nassert_eq!(vec, [1, 2, 3]);\n\nTime complexityTakes amortized O(1) time. If the vector's length would exceed its capacity after the push, O(capacity) time is taken to copy the vector's elements to a larger allocation. This expensive operation is offset by the capacity O(1) insertions it allows."
  },
