   {
    "detail": "fn(&mut self) -> Option<T>",
    "documentation": {
     "kind": "markdown",
     "value": "Removes the last element from a vector and returns it, or [`None`] if it\nis empty.\n\nIf you'd like to pop the first element, consider using\n[`VecDeque::pop_front`] instead.\n\n[`VecDeque::pop_front`]: crate::collections::VecDeque::pop_front\n\n# Examples\n\n```rust\nlet mut vec = vec![1, 2, 3];\nassert_eq!(vec.pop(), Some(3));\nassert_eq!(vec, [1, 2]);\n```\n\n# Time complexity\n\nTakes *O*(1) time."
    },
